          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "suspīrō is built on sub- \"up from below\" and spīrō \"to breathe\" (Lewis & Short; EtymDB): a sigh is a breath drawn up from deep down. English inspire and respire share spīrō."
            }
          ]
        },
